      "comment": "ULTIMATE ZIPPER (5) was in the money two runs ago then went well again last time over 2100m at Bunbury, finishing 15 metres from the winner in second. Primary contender based on those recent efforts. WRITE RITE RIGHT (3) won at Bunbury two runs ago but couldn't repeat the dose at his latest appearance over 2100m at Bunbury, beaten 5.5 metres. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Won't find this any harder and he can get back to the winner's list. BETTOR BE BUCKS (1) has been thereabouts of late and is a great chance to break through. Good effort last time out when she finished third at Northam over 2190m. DUNCAN TWENTYTWO (6) was unplaced two starts ago then things went wrong last start when he broke and finished 13 metres away in fourth over 2130m at Gloucester Park. Finds a nice race and can make up for that last start mishap.",
